#############################################################################
# Weathra frontend configuration
#
# Copy to frontend/.env.local and fill in.
#
# Everything here is PUBLIC. A NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix ships the value in the
# browser bundle, so only the Supabase project URL, its public client key, and
# the backend base URL may appear in this file.
#
# The Supabase service-role key, the database URLs, and the inference key are
# backend secrets. They must never be added here under any name, prefixed or
# not — CI asserts their absence from the frontend environment and the built
# bundle (design.md decision 19).
#############################################################################

# Supabase project URL.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co

# Supabase public client key (the anon key, or its publishable-key equivalent).
# Public by design: it carries no privilege beyond what Row Level Security and
# Supabase Auth allow an anonymous or signed-in caller to do.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key

# Weathra backend base URL. Changing it retargets the frontend with no code
# change, so the two applications can sit on different origins or later behind
# one domain.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000

#############################################################################
# City imagery — configured elsewhere, on purpose
#
# The Dashboard hero and the Compare Cities banners resolve a photograph for
# the place they are showing, through three tiers: a provider photograph, a
# photograph committed to public/locations/photos/, and the artwork this
# repository draws. All of it is optional — with nothing configured the chain
# starts at tier two and every screen still renders.
#
# The provider's credential is a SECRET, so it is deliberately not documented
# in this file and must never be added to it. Everything here is public by
# definition, and scripts/secret-containment.test.ts enforces that by refusing
# any name not on its permitted list — which is the check working, not an
# obstacle to route around.
#
# It is read only by lib/images/provider.server.ts, which refuses to load in a
# browser, and reached only through /api/location-image. See
# docs/city-imagery.md for the variable names and how to set them.
#############################################################################

#############################################################################
# What is deliberately absent
#
# **The backend's secrets.** The service-role key, the database connection
# strings, and the inference credential are server-side only. They belong in
# `backend/.env` locally and in server-side deployment secret storage in
# production — Google Cloud Secret Manager, surfaced as Cloud Run environment
# secrets — never in this application's environment, its build, or Git.
#
# **The design tool (Visily.ai).** It is a design-time tool that produces the
# artifacts recorded under `docs/design/` — as did UXPilot, the earlier
# exploration whose approved design direction Visily carries forward. Nothing
# in the running frontend calls either, so neither has a variable here and
# neither needs a key of any kind at runtime.
#############################################################################
